From 7830afe3946443605b36eaded9f0b89c294080a2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 13:58:48 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Scenario 5: publication by generation + manifest, for Hydra
 ETL and Airflow

The recipe suggested by Tim Urista: each run writes into its own directory and
one manifest file is switched at the end; readers resolve the manifest once.
hydra_gen/ (no change to the engine) and daily_revenue_safe_gen.py share
shared/publish_generation.py. crash_scenario.py gets --manifest, a reader that
resolves the manifest, and a kill sent when a new generation holds its first
report. Measured in a Linux sandbox, not on the EC2 machine.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011X5H6WN7YFXx8LCdr73MxR
